      "prompt": "A single flat-sided hexagonal diorama tile, 32 m across, lush meadow grass cap and the hexagon side walls show a thin grass lip over dark root-filled topsoil that darkens softly downward into a near-black foot, one continuous dark earth, with one small two-storey village cottage shop in the timber-framed English cottage style: dark oak half-timbering over cream lime-plaster panels, a steep brown clay-tile roof with gables, tall red-brick chimneys with clay pots, and small-paned timber casement windows. Its ground-floor front is a wide small-paned timber bow window full of crusty loaves, round cobs, plaited loaves and buns on wooden shelves and in wicker baskets, beside a half-glazed timber shop door under a small clay-tile canopy, with a wicker basket of bread on a bench by the door and flower boxes under the upper windows. The beam above the bow window is plain dark oak like the rest of the framing. The building stands on a flagstone forecourt that meets one flat edge of the tile square-on, where it joins a short stub of 6 m wide two-lane asphalt country road, faded dashed white centre line, low concrete kerbs, grass verges with tufts and small bushes, stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, soft noon sun, neutral grey studio background, 35 degree three-quarter view"
